{"id":"comprehend","corpus":"aws","title":"Amazon Comprehend","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/what-is.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"Amazon Comprehend"},{"kind":"p","text":"Amazon Comprehend uses natural language processing (NLP) to extract insights about the content of documents. It develops insights by recognizing the entities, key phrases, language, sentiments, and other common elements in a document. Use Amazon Comprehend to create new products based on understanding the structure of documents. For example, using Amazon Comprehend you can search social networking feeds for mentions of products or scan an entire document repository for key phrases."},{"kind":"p","text":"You can access Amazon Comprehend document analysis capabilities using the Amazon Comprehend console or using the Amazon Comprehend APIs. You can run real-time analysis for small workloads or you can start asynchronous analysis jobs for large document sets. You can use the pre-trained models that Amazon Comprehend provides, or you can train your own custom models for classification and entity recognition."},{"kind":"p","text":"Amazon Comprehend may store your content to continuously improve the quality of its pre-trained models. See the Amazon Comprehend FAQ to learn more."},{"kind":"p","text":"All of the Amazon Comprehend features accept UTF-8 text documents as the input. In addition, custom classification and custom entity recognition accept image files, PDF files, and Word files as input."},{"kind":"p","text":"Amazon Comprehend can examine and analyze documents in a variety of languages, depending on the specific feature. For more information, see Languages supported in Amazon Comprehend. Amazon Comprehend's Dominant language capability can examine documents and determine the dominant language for a far wider selection of languages."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Amazon Comprehend insights"},{"kind":"p","text":"Amazon Comprehend uses a pre-trained model to examine and analyze a document or set of documents to gather insights about it. This model is continuously trained on a large body of text so that there is no need for you to provide training data."},{"kind":"p","text":"Amazon Comprehend analyzes the following types of insights:"},{"kind":"li","text":"Entities – References to the names of people, places, items, and locations contained in a document."},{"kind":"li","text":"Key phrases – Phrases that appear in a document. For example, a document about a basketball game might return the names of the teams, the name of the venue, and the final score."},{"kind":"li","text":"Personally Identifiable Information (PII) – Personal data that can identify an individual, such as an address, bank account number, or phone number."},{"kind":"li","text":"Language – The dominant language of a document."},{"kind":"li","text":"Sentiment – The dominant sentiment of a document, which can be positive, neutral, negative, or mixed."},{"kind":"li","text":"Targeted sentiment – The sentiments associated with specific entities in a document. The sentiment for each entity occurrence can be positive, negative, neutral or mixed."},{"kind":"li","text":"Syntax – The parts of speech for each word in the document."},{"kind":"p","text":"For more information, see Insights."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Amazon Comprehend Custom"},{"kind":"p","text":"You can customize Amazon Comprehend for your specific requirements without the skillset required to build machine learning-based NLP solutions. Using automatic machine learning, or AutoML, Amazon Comprehend Custom builds customized NLP models on your behalf, using data you already have."},{"kind":"p","text":"Custom classification – Create custom classification models (classifiers) to organize your documents into your own categories."},{"kind":"p","text":"Custom entity recognition – Create custom entity recognition models (recognizers) that can analyze text for your specific terms and noun-based phrases."},{"kind":"p","text":"For more information, see Amazon Comprehend Custom."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Flywheels"},{"kind":"p","text":"Use flywheels to simplify the process of training and managing custom model versions over time. A flywheel helps to orchestrate the tasks associated with training and evaluating new versions of a model. Flywheels support plain-text custom models for custom classification and custom entity recognition. For more information, see Flywheels."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Document clustering (topic modeling)"},{"kind":"p","text":"You can also use Amazon Comprehend to examine a corpus of documents to organize them based on similar keywords within them. Document clustering (topic modeling) is useful to organize a large corpus of documents into topics or clusters that are similar based on word frequency. For more information, see Topic modeling."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Examples"},{"kind":"p","text":"The following examples show how you might use the Amazon Comprehend operations in your applications."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Example 1: Find documents about a subject"},{"kind":"p","text":"Find the documents about a particular subject using Amazon Comprehend topic modeling. Scan a set of documents to determine the topics discussed, and to find the documents associated with each topic. You can specify the number of topics that Amazon Comprehend should return from the document set."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Example 2: Find out how customers feel about your products"},{"kind":"p","text":"If your company publishes a catalog, let Amazon Comprehend tell you what customers think of your products. Send each customer comment to the DetectSentiment operation and it will tell you whether customers feel positive, negative, neutral, or mixed about a product."}],"lemmas":{"amazons":["amazon","amazons"],"comprehends":["comprehends","comprehend"],"uses":["use","uses"],"used":["used","use"],"naturals":["natural","naturals"],"processing":["process